>> title: Ful Medames, Instant Pot
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: fava beans, egyptian, breakfast, cumin, vegan, instant pot, pressure cooker, no soak
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot ful medames, pressure cooker ful, no soak fava beans, foul medames, ful mudammas, fool medames, fava beans, Egyptian breakfast beans
>> servings: 4
>> dish: ful-medames
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> pairs-with: pita-bread, labneh, kabis
>> time: 1 hr 35 min
>> slack: unforgiving — a fava that does not flatten under a spoon is undercooked; lock the lid again for ten more rather than serve them like that

>> step: cook from dry, no soak — 45 min at high pressure
Put @dried fava beans{1 1/2%cups}(300 g; small brown ful, dry — not soaked, not the big pale broad bean) into the #Instant Pot{} with @water{5%cups}(1.2 L), @bay leaf{1} and @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, lock the lid and ~pressure cook{45%min} at high pressure.

>> step: wait out the natural release 20 min
Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{20%min} until the pin drops on its own.

>> step: crush about half against the pot
Crush about half of @&(~1)cooked beans{} against the side of the inner pot and leave the rest whole, ladling off most of the water first and stirring a little back in.

>> step: dress with lemon, oil and cumin
Dress @&(~1)crushed beans{} with @lemon juice{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @extra-virgin olive oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed to a paste), @ground cumin{2%tsp} and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}, stirring hard so it goes glossy.

>> step: build the top, finish at the table
Turn @&(~1)dressed ful{} into a shallow bowl and build @ripe tomato{1}(diced), @flat-leaf parsley{1/4%cup}(chopped), @red onion{1/4}(diced fine) and @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) over the top, with @lemon{1}(in wedges) and more cumin alongside.
